_auto,q_auto/556846e095b6358720fcfa526f7014fb","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-02T17:28:11.265Z"},{"id":"AzhqZl3q5","title":"Prisma support for CockroachDB is now in Preview","url":"https://www.prisma.io/blog/prisma-preview-cockroach-db-release","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/prisma-support-for-cockroachdb-is-now-in-preview-azhqzl3q5","summary":"Prisma is a next-generation open-source ORM for Node.js and TypeScript. It helps you be more productive and confident when developing database-driven applications. CockroachDB is a distributed SQL database that shines in its ability to scale efficiently while maintaining developer agility and reducing operational overhead.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/622e84f5c29f99b370bd06a82536ed7d","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-02T17:26:13.358Z"},{"id":"UdNsAW648","title":"Block Protocol","url":"https://blockprotocol.org/?ref=console.dev","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/block-protocol-udnsaw648","summary":"The Block Protocol specification provides a set of guidelines on how to write blocks that render, create, update, and delete data in a predictable way. This standardization makes it possible to easily move both blocks and data between applications that adhere to the protocol. The Block Protocol makes interoperable, block-based data possible.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3e9530c7807d474ed7fce6af022f7f7a","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-02T17:24:02.148Z"},{"id":"evdNE51a2","title":"Announcing Go 1.18 Beta 2","url":"https://go.dev/blog/go1.18beta2?ref=console.dev","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-go-1-18-beta-2-evdne51a2","summary":"Go 1.18 beta 1 is now the most downloaded Go beta ever, with twice as many downloads as any previous release. Beta 1 helped us identify obscure bugs in the new support for generics and ensure a more stable final release. The Go language server gopls and the VS Code Go extension now support generics.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--P4t4XyoV--/f_auto/v1722860399/public/Placeholder%2001","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-02T17:24:00.245Z"},{"id":"P5fze6OeE","title":"Layercode","url":"https://layercode.com/usecsv?ref=console.dev","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/layercode-p5fze6oee","summary":"Validation happens before data is imported to your app. Users can fix validation issues seamlessly without having to go back into Excel. Our in-browser spreadsheet editor means users can fix errors immediately. We hope you will use this tool to help you with your app's data validation.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c24f55ccf5e62fe09b5520dae32b9593","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-02T17:21:49.707Z"},{"id":"eVZsj0gsh","title":"Search more with less","url":"https://quickwit.io","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/search-more-with-less-evzsj0gsh","summary":"Quickwit builds and delivers community-based software that is open and free. We understand that building and maintaining an end-to-end search and analytics solution is already tedious enough without having to add vendor lock ins or black box architectures. We believe a company's success lays in its ability to hone all of its data. Search is only the beginning.","image":"https://quickwit.io/favicons/apple-icon-57x57.png","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-27T12:26:22.047Z"},{"id":"IxslomEgi","title":"soketi","url":"https://docs.soketi.app/?ref=console.dev","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/soketi-ixslomegi","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/bf278274601ea90c2e7e319de37b0c6e","num_upvotes":24,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2022-01-27T12:25:56.658Z"},{"id":"Oh1GjGUMj","title":"Primitives \u2014 Radix UI","url":"https://radix-ui.com","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/primitives-radix-ui-oh1gjgumj","summary":"Each component is its own independently versioned package, so new components can be added alongside your existing code. No need to disrupt feature work with a huge rewrite. You can start small and add more components one by one. Incremental adoption can be achieved by adding new components one at a time.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f70116fbf524d1a1e89adfdb8a0febd6","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-25T14:57:20.599Z"},{"id":"MYTYnlfeH","title":"Interactive Documentation","url":"https://www.usedevbook.com/?ref=console.dev","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/interactive-documentation-mytynlfeh","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ec342d1056403026650b5bc03d41fffb","num_upvotes":7,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-25T14:55:17.252Z"},{"id":"qYGrhEFe6","title":"Introducing Rainway: Interactive App Streaming for Everyone","url":"https://rainway.com/blog/2022/01/25/rainway-sdk-public-release/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-rainway-interactive-app-streaming-for-everyone-qygrhefe6","summary":"Rainway is a platform for building real-time, interactive web apps with embedded native applications. Our zero trust app streaming technology makes it possible for even the heaviest native apps, or an entire operating system (OS), to run on any platform. It integrates seamlessly into existing frontend frameworks such as React, and can be deployed on public cloud infrastructure.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/47a22c70c725c85340cd6a4e5726c481","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-01-25T00:00:00.000Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"Bf4cTugEF","title":"Astro","url":"https://astro.build","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/astro-bf4ctugef","summary":"Astro lets you use any framework you want (or none at all) Build faster websites with less client-side Javascript and more HTML and CSS. We\u2019re not the first to ask the question, but we might be the first with an answer for every framework. Keep your eyes to the skies, astronauts.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/4c06869d5fb85dffa2d0d9bb0a2a83e2","num_upvotes":93,"num_comments":6,"created_at":"2021-06-09T15:00:14.625Z"},{"id":"DA-b9W6br","title":"Framer: Design beautiful websites in minutes","url":"https://www.framer.com/sites/?ref=console.dev","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/framer-design-beautiful-websites-in-minutes-da-b9w6br","summary":null,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/c99df2131d28846e6cd6ce1768104eec","num_upvotes":70,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2022-01-20T08:25:10.336Z"},{"id":"W2IILBl4R","title":"storybookjs/storybook: \ud83d\udcd3 The UI component explorer. Develop, document, & test React, Vue, Angular, Web Components, Ember, Svelte & more!","url":"https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/storybookjs-storybook-the-ui-component-explorer-develop-document-test-react-vue-angular-w-w2iilbl4r","summary":"Storybook is a development environment for UI components. It allows you to browse a component library, view the different states of each component, and interactively develop and test components. Storybook's API makes it possible to configure and extend in various ways. It has been extended to support React Native, Android, iOS, and Flutter development for mobile.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/539f5c8478124e59686bba8183047688","num_upvotes":48,"num_comments":6,"created_at":"2021-11-03T11:13:43.868Z"},{"id":"TWZqKX7h8","title":"Tamagui \u2014 React Native + Web UI kit","url":"https://tamagui.dev","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/tamagui-react-native-web-ui-kit-twzqkx7h8","s